In article <tkevans.759336415@eplrx7.es.dupont.com>, tkevans@eplrx7.es.duPont.com (Tim Evans) writes:

>I'm mostly a Sun/IBM RS6000 admin, but have an Alpha with OSF1 as a
>demo.  The DEC tech set it up, and I've lost/forgotten the root password.
>How do you boot OSF1 single-user?  Thanks.

  Halt the system, and at the >>> console prompt, type:

	SET BOOT_OSFLAGS ""<return>  The double quotes are required!

  Boot the system:

	B<return>

  System will boot to single user mode.

  To boot from single user to multi-user mode:

	init 3<return>

  Halt the system, su, then type:

	shutdown -h now

  At the >>> colsole prompt, type:

	SET BOOT_OSFLAGS "A"

  This will reconfigure the system to <A>utomatically boot multi-user.

Cheers
