In "include/Master.Config.File" I added:

BBCFLAGS="....... -D_BSD"
BBLIB="........ -lbsd"

Note that "......." means whatever you already had and then add what
you see I added. This is the easy way out. You could go through and
take care of all the problems that would arise, and I think there are
several others. Of course, our version of FreePort might be an an older
one and we have made many local changes. Also, our port was from ULTRIX
4.3 to OSF 1.3A. I had to make a lot of fixes and changes from the
original code to ULTRIX 4.3. I think the original code was done on a
RS6000. The people who wrote FreePort were very helpfull with answering
questions I had when I did the original port to ULTRIX.

