In article <1994Jan24.133417.5574@porthos.cc.bellcore.com>, kenton@navahonavaho.cc.bellcore.com (gidewall,kenton c) writes:
>We are interested in running SLIP or PPP via phone lines on our VAXstation
>3100s (VMS 5.5-2).  I would like to hear any feedback from people, especially
>on the following questions:
>
>Which is better, SLIP or PPP? (I'm assuming the answer is PPP, from what
>I've read)

Depends on what you're trying to do (if you only need IP, SLIP should be
just fine), and if it is available.

>What are the best commercial packages available for each?

DECserver 700s, 900s, and some of the 90's support SLIP and PPP.  MultiNet
(sales@tgv.com) and TCPware (sales@process.com) include SLIP.  I'm sure 
other TCP/IP implementations for VMS (like Wollongong's, sales@twg.com)
have SLIP as well.  DEC's UCX doesn't include SLIP.

I don't know of any PPP implementations for VMS.

>Are there any PD versions available on the net?  I haven't been able to
>find any.

I believe that is because there aren't any (for VMS).

