>a large file can effectively flush out all the instruction/data pages.

The default value for "ubc_maxpercent" (the maximum percentage of system
memory that is allocated to the dynamic buffer cache) is 100%. If you
want to avoid the situation above, change that kernel parameter to something
smaller (I normally keep it around 60 %).

