You'll love the answer to this one. OSF on DEC supports bith BSD4.3 and
BSD4.4 network structures. For the most part programs don't care which
you use, but for using mount - you need the BSD4.4 one....

I placed the following in my program before the header files and all
worked:

/* The following hack is required for OSF/1 on the alpha as it turns on the
   BSD 4.4 network sockaddr_in which is used by the kernel NFS mount.
   See netinet/in.h.... Essentially, the len and family fields were
   merged and we were trampling over things....
   (This is for OSF 1.3)
 */
#if defined(__osf__)
#define _SOCKADDR_LEN 1
#endif


	Have fun....

	Ezra




