|> on a 3000/600. Only one would run at once (ie one would seem to pause while
|> the other was doing something). Surely 32MB is enough for 2 users to 
|> compile a program?

As stated in a previous post, you might want to reduce ubc_maxpercent
in /usr/sys/conf/param.c and rebuild and reboot your kernel.  This
controls the percentage of main memory that the filesystem can consume.  
Jobs like compilers that are both I/O and cpu intensive tend to start
battles between the filesystem and the vm, and reducing ubc_maxpercent
allows the vm to keep more pages for program text and data.

Also, others have reported that with the current versions of OSF/1,
32 mb is kind of on the small side, believe it or not.

