In article <2h3oac$frl@server.cs.vt.edu>, root@vtopus.cs.vt.edu (System PRIVILEGED Account) writes:

>Does OSF V1.2a support the DSP5400 drive (from Applied Digital Systems)?
>If so, could someone send me the pertinent info (like disktab entry or
>such)?  If not, will OSF V1.3 support it?

As a rule Digital only supported qualified Digital drives.  Support
in this context is a special word quite different from "it should
work".  It means the drive has been throughly qualified on the system
with all other devices that are also supported.  There is also some
hardware qualification dependent on the platform that ensures the
drive is kept cool enough, doesn't sound like a radio station, etc.

That said, the DSP5400 looks a whole lot like the RZ74 which is
supported on V1.3 on the DEC 4000s.  This bit of information was
gotten from the V1.3 SPD which is the official document of what
is and is not Supported.

Being so much like the RZ74, the DSP5400 is likely to be very
well behaved and should work.  Even if V1.3 or V1.2a doesn't
have a disktab entry for it, don't worry; you don't need one.
If you use a disk type that disklabel doesn't know about when
you label the disk it will get the geometry and partition 
information from the driver.  This this information filled in
newfs(8) doesn't need the disk type.

