In article <2h6msi$nd1@server.cs.vt.edu>, lat@server.cs.vt.edu (Laurie Zirkle) writes:

>The only other question
>I have is what is the largest partition size supported under OSF V1.2a
>and OSF v1.3 or where can I find that information?

The V1.2 SPD had a 40 GB maximum file system size limit.  I don't
know if more recent SPDs have had a limit documented.  For use as
a raw device the partition size is limited to around 8,000,000 TB.
For a file system the size is bounded by the use of triple indirect
blocks and the number of block as a signed 32 bit number.  In other
words BIG.

I don't know anywhere in V1.x where this information might be documented.
It has to be derived from knowing what fields of what data structures are
likely to limit the size.
