In article <1994Jan14.164003.57216@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu>,
anh@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu writes:

[...]
anh> #include <stdarg.h>
[...]
anh> void test(format)
anh> char *format;
anh> {
anh>   va_list vlist;
[...]

Your function declaration is incorrect--it *must* be

void test(char *format, ...)

See the ANSI C standard, section 6.7.1, "Semantics":

   "If a function that accepts a variable number of arguments is
    defined without a parameter type list that ends with the ellipsis
    notation, the result is undefined."

Fix that, and you should find that it works fine.

