The DECUS U S Chapter Languages and Tools Team invites you to
participate in the Spring 1994 Symposia in New Orleans, LA, May 9th
through 12th, 1994.  L&T is particularly interested in presentations
around our central theme:

     "Meeting the Challenges of Multiplatform Development"

We would very much like to see sessions on:

     - Porting "legacy" systems to new architectures
     - Mixed-architecture client-server solutions
     - Compiler compatability and differences across platforms
     - New platforms, particularly Alpha and Window-based systems

However, general sessions on the use of languages and tools, in
particular tutorial and case-study sessions, are also needed, and
we encourage their submission.

The deadline for submission is only two weeks away:

                    Tuesday, February 1st, 1994!


To get a copy of the complete CFP and information about the format
of the event:


        - Call 1-800-DECUS55 and ask to have a CFP form sent to you
        - Use anonymous ftp to decus.org, and get a copy
          from [.DECUS94-NEWORLEANS]CFP.TXT
        - Send an e-mail message to mailserv@decus.org with the line
                SEND [DECUS94-NEWORLEANS]CFP.TXT
          in the message body (not the subject line).

Once you have completed the CFP you may:
        - Send it via US mail (address is in the CFP)
        - Fax it to 508-841-3357
        - Send it via e-mail to information@decus.org

Note that the CFP identifies certain core tracks, but L&T is working to
add to the total event.  If your session does not fit into a core track,
please submit it anyway, so that we'll have a wide variety of sessions
to offer.

         Again, the close of CFP is Tuesday, February 1st.

If you have questions about L&T specifically, please contact:

  Tom Comeau, L&T Chair, <tcomeau@stsci.edu>
or
  Barb Nicholson, L&T Stream Coordinator, <nicholson%44540@randb.abbott.com>

We hope you'll participate in our New Orleans/'94 program!

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tom Comeau, Languages and Tools SIG Chair
tcomeau@stsci.edu
