of the researchers here at umass, i was wondering if
anyone had a solution.

-- craig

-------
 
 On the alphas, there is a bug, which I believe is in the X server
 software, but it is most annoying while running emacs.
 
 There are two bugs.  The first one is that in emacs (and I think other
 applciations), if you hold down one key till it auto-repeats and then
 hit another key after it quickly, the second key will auto-repeat.
 
 The second is that certain combinations of modifier keys will behave
 incorrectly.  If you hold down control-shift, for instance to do
 control-shift-_ (undo in emacs), then even if you let go of the
 control-shift, the next key will be shifted, in fact, there will be a
 shift-lock in effect until you hit some modifier key by itself to
 cancel the modifier state.  This is incredibly annoying as much of
 what we do uses multiple modifier keys in emacs.
 




