The following small Fortran program executes woefully slow on a DEC Alpha
OSF1.3 with DEC Fortran compiler V3.3-342:
      program ex
      implicit none
      real*8 fi,ans /0.0/
      integer i
      do i=1,100000
         fi=float(i)
         ans=ans+((0.5**fi)/(fi**1.5))
      enddo
      write (6,*) ans
      stop
      end
Running under OSF1.3 is about 4 times slower than on a DEC Station 5000/150
with Ultrix V4.3. I would have expected the opposite to be the case based
on past benchmarks. Exactly the same thing happens when the equivalent C
code is used, making me suspect that the coding for exponentiation in the
C library is woefully slow. Has anybody else noticed this and more
specifically does DEC have a fix for this?

