hirai@cc.swarthmore.edu (Eiji Hirai) writes:

[...stuff deleted...]
>> The only odd thing about the entire installation is the result of doing a 
>> show dev at the monitor level.  On the SCSI bus, it shows both the appropriate
>> complement of disks, and the tape drive.  However, the tape drive entry is
>> repeated 8 times, with devices numbers of B/4/0, B/4/1, B/4/2, ....  B/4/7.
[...stuff deleted...]

I had this effect, too (EXABYTE 8500, OSF/1 1.3). The cause was that
both the tape drive and the host itself had the same SCSI address (6).
In this case, the machine gets totally confused and sees six and more
tape drives :-)
On our AXP 400, the host ID for both SCSI buses is 6 (six) by default.

You can determine your host's SCSI addresses by doing a "show SCSI_A"
and "show SCSI_B" at monitor level. You can also change the IDs by means
of the SET command, but I don't know if this will hang the machine...


Hope this helps, and best regards, Christian Rang


