manu@ecstasy.cemes.fr (Emmanuel Courcelle) writes:
>Hello.
>I 'm trying compiling Wcl-2.5 on a Digital Workstation running Dec OSF/1 1.3
>Here the tail of the make output:
>cc  -o Ari Ari.o ...
>ld:
>Unresolved:
>dnet_conn
>dnet_addr
>getnodebyname
>*** Exit 1
>Stop.

From memory, this was caused by the WCL Makefile explicitly telling the
linker to look in /usr/lib (-L/usr/lib), which is where the staticly
linked binaries are. Solutions:

1) Fix the Makefiles, so it doesnt have -L/usr/lib, it will then look
in /usr/shlib, where it should. This will also make the final binaries
dynamically linked, rather than static, which will save a lot of diskspace.

or

2) add -ldnet_stub to the tail of the list of libraries.

The first is the better solution. Apart from the above problem, I 
_seem_ to recall WCL compiled fine on the alphas.

